{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":20959,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"999185e6-3dcf-5748-bad3-bfe0f3005ec3","total_cost_usd":0.28391999999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9636,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1722,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9636,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1722,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9636},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5005,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00508,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1722,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9636,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27884,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"absence\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":\"not-applicable-no-lock\",\"reasons\":[\"Declared independent-unit column crab_id is consistent with the frozen data: exactly 12 distinct crab_id values (CM-01..CM-12), each appearing in exactly 4 rows (two quiet, two vessel_noise sessions), totalling the stated 48 rows; per-animal attributes (carapace_width_mm, tank_bay) are constant within each crab_id, confirming rows within a crab are repeated measurements on one unit rather than separate units.\",\"Both arms of the paired procedure are within-crab: every crab contributes both quiet and vessel_noise sessions, so crab_id is the correct pairing unit and no between-crab confounding of the declared unit with condition exists.\",\"The workflow collapses sessions within crab per condition (collapse_within_crab enforces exactly 2 sessions per condition per crab) before running stats.ttest_rel, so the row-independent procedure receives exactly one paired value per independent unit.\",\"The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue explicitly: it states the test uses 12 paired values, one per crab, reports n = 12 crabs and df = 11 (t(11) = 8.5896) rather than degrees of freedom tracking the 48 session rows, and includes the crab-level means table showing the collapse.\",\"Independent recomputation from data/input.csv confirms the reported figures: per-crab quiet/noise means match the table, mean within-crab difference = 8.00 beats/min, SD = 3.23, SE ≈ 0.931, t ≈ 8.59 with df = 11, and all 12 differences positive, matching the signed-rank check (W = 0).\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock conformance is not applicable.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column crab_id is consistent with the frozen data: exactly 12 distinct crab_id values (CM-01..CM-12), each appearing in exactly 4 rows (two quiet, two vessel_noise sessions), totalling the stated 48 rows; per-animal attributes (carapace_width_mm, tank_bay) are constant within each crab_id, confirming rows within a crab are repeated measurements on one unit rather than separate units.","Both arms of the paired procedure are within-crab: every crab contributes both quiet and vessel_noise sessions, so crab_id is the correct pairing unit and no between-crab confounding of the declared unit with condition exists.","The workflow collapses sessions within crab per condition (collapse_within_crab enforces exactly 2 sessions per condition per crab) before running stats.ttest_rel, so the row-independent procedure receives exactly one paired value per independent unit.","The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue explicitly: it states the test uses 12 paired values, one per crab, reports n = 12 crabs and df = 11 (t(11) = 8.5896) rather than degrees of freedom tracking the 48 session rows, and includes the crab-level means table showing the collapse.","Independent recomputation from data/input.csv confirms the reported figures: per-crab quiet/noise means match the table, mean within-crab difference = 8.00 beats/min, SD = 3.23, SE ≈ 0.931, t ≈ 8.59 with df = 11, and all 12 differences positive, matching the signed-rank check (W = 0).","No authority lock was minted, so lock conformance is not applicable."]},"ttft_ms":9053,"ttft_stream_ms":1782,"time_to_request_ms":12,"type":"result","duration_ms":21670,"uuid":"4a4d4ab7-be8f-4fd0-844d-488f5f594063"}
